160
00:08:42,060 --> 00:08:47,060
Uh, I wanted to know the secret to making a great movie.

161
00:08:47,060 --> 00:08:49,060
Hmm? Hmm.

162
00:08:49,060 --> 00:08:52,060
There's no real correct way to make a movie.

163
00:08:52,060 --> 00:08:54,060
Oh, yeah, right.

164
00:08:54,060 --> 00:08:58,060
But a film set is a living thing.

165
00:08:58,060 --> 00:09:04,060
From the actors' moods to the changing scenes, you need to have a sharp eye.

166
00:09:04,060 --> 00:09:08,060
That way, you'll never miss a moment that sparkles.

167
00:09:08,060 --> 00:09:11,060
I need to have a sharp eye. Got it.

168
00:09:11,060 --> 00:09:16,060
And I'm guessing you're asking because you hope to make your own movie one day?

169
00:09:16,060 --> 00:09:20,060
What? No! No way! I could never! Not in my wildest dreams!

170
00:09:20,060 --> 00:09:25,060
There, there. You've gotta relax, son.

171
00:09:25,060 --> 00:09:28,060
There's a reason Pumpo chose you to be on her team.

172
00:09:28,060 --> 00:09:30,060
Huh? Uh, she what?

173
00:09:30,060 --> 00:09:35,060
Look, a producer's job is basically all about spotting talent.

174
00:09:35,060 --> 00:09:39,060
Have you considered that the reason Pumpo keeps you around

175
00:09:39,060 --> 00:09:43,060
is because she sees something in you? Hmm?

176
00:09:43,060 --> 00:09:46,060
Wait. You mean... really?

177
00:09:48,060 --> 00:09:49,060
Hmm.

178
00:09:49,060 --> 00:09:51,060
I think you're right. It would make a good adaptation.

179
00:09:51,060 --> 00:09:52,060
Hey, Mr. Director.

180
00:09:52,060 --> 00:09:53,060
Hmm?

181
00:09:53,060 --> 00:09:54,060
A word?

182
00:09:54,060 --> 00:09:56,060
It's decided.

183
00:09:56,060 --> 00:09:58,060
That is correct, Gene, my boy.

184
00:09:58,060 --> 00:10:01,060
You will be cutting the trailer for Marine.

185
00:10:01,060 --> 00:10:03,060
Wh- Whaaaaat?

186
00:10:03,060 --> 00:10:07,060
But, but, but, but doesn't a producer usually hire a special trailer house

187
00:10:07,060 --> 00:10:08,060
to do something like that?

188
00:10:08,060 --> 00:10:10,060
You wanna make movies, right?

189
00:10:10,060 --> 00:10:14,060
Well, you gotta take risks and not do what everyone else usually does.

190
00:10:14,060 --> 00:10:21,060
Hmm. Hmm. Hmm. Hmm.

191
00:10:21,060 --> 00:10:23,060
I'm gonna need you to cut a 15-second spot.

192
00:10:23,060 --> 00:10:25,060
You know how to use editing software, right?

193
00:10:25,060 --> 00:10:28,060
Well, yes, but...

194
00:10:28,060 --> 00:10:30,060
Grab their attention right from the top.

195
00:10:30,060 --> 00:10:33,060
Give them a taste of some of the best parts,

196
00:10:33,060 --> 00:10:35,060
but mislead them to create buzz.

197
00:10:35,060 --> 00:10:36,060
And then...

198
00:10:36,060 --> 00:10:38,060
End of the thing!

199
00:10:38,060 --> 00:10:40,060
Something like that.

200
00:10:40,060 --> 00:10:42,060
All that in just 15 seconds?

201
00:10:42,060 --> 00:10:43,060
Yup.

202
00:10:43,060 --> 00:10:47,060
The 15-second trailer teaser is the spot that most people will see,

203
00:10:47,060 --> 00:10:49,060
which means it also directly affects the box office.

204
00:10:49,060 --> 00:10:52,060
The livelihoods of the entire crew and their families

205
00:10:52,060 --> 00:10:54,060
lie solely in your hands now. Got it?

206
00:10:54,060 --> 00:11:07,060
It is simply impossible to realistically fit all of that into just 15 seconds.

207
00:11:07,060 --> 00:11:09,060
That's not enough time.

208
00:11:09,060 --> 00:11:13,060
That's why I'm going to include outside footage.

209
00:11:13,060 --> 00:11:31,060
One technique of filmmaking

210
00:11:31,060 --> 00:11:35,060
is to make the audience imagine the next scene without showing it.

211
00:11:35,060 --> 00:11:48,060
They don't have to show everything.

212
00:11:48,060 --> 00:11:51,060
I'll let the audience fill in the gaps in their heads.

213
00:11:51,060 --> 00:11:55,060
I'm not even thinking about box office or the crew's livelihoods right now.

214
00:11:55,060 --> 00:11:58,060
Because I'm having too much fun!

215
00:12:20,060 --> 00:12:23,060
It was supposed to be another typical vacation.

216
00:12:25,060 --> 00:12:38,060
Well, so what do you think?

217
