242
00:13:47,060 --> 00:13:48,060
Hmm?

243
00:13:48,060 --> 00:13:52,060
I was wondering why you decided to make me your assistant.

244
00:13:52,060 --> 00:13:54,060
There are so many others.

245
00:13:54,060 --> 00:13:57,060
People who have better schooling, better looking,

246
00:13:57,060 --> 00:13:59,060
are just all around better than me.

247
00:13:59,060 --> 00:14:01,060
So then, what made you choose me?

248
00:14:01,060 --> 00:14:03,060
Ah, that's an easy one.

249
00:14:03,060 --> 00:14:04,060
Huh?

250
00:14:04,060 --> 00:14:07,060
People possess one quality that nobody else has.

251
00:14:10,060 --> 00:14:11,060
Your eyes.

252
00:14:11,060 --> 00:14:12,060
Don't sparkle!

253
00:14:12,060 --> 00:14:13,060
Huh?

254
00:14:13,060 --> 00:14:14,060
Huh?

255
00:14:14,060 --> 00:14:16,060
If you take a look into everyone else's eyes,

256
00:14:16,060 --> 00:14:20,060
they sparkle brilliantly with the hope of adolescent optimism.

257
00:14:20,060 --> 00:14:24,060
But the truth is, a fulfilling life gives you a perspective

258
00:14:24,060 --> 00:14:26,060
that lacks a certain depth.

259
00:14:26,060 --> 00:14:28,060
And so happiness destroys creativity.

260
00:14:28,060 --> 00:14:31,060
So those others aren't qualified to be creators.

261
00:14:31,060 --> 00:14:35,060
However, when I looked into your eyes,

262
00:14:35,060 --> 00:14:40,060
I saw the typical signs of an outcast with nothing going for him.

263
00:14:40,060 --> 00:14:42,060
That's a compliment.

264
00:14:42,060 --> 00:14:44,060
Uh, thank you?

265
00:14:44,060 --> 00:14:47,060
People who don't fit in the real world

266
00:14:47,060 --> 00:14:50,060
