That was my first time working out.

561
00:27:04,160 --> 00:27:05,900
My whole body hurts.

562
00:27:05,900 --> 00:27:12,280
Leave the cooking to me.

563
00:27:13,340 --> 00:27:15,240
It's the least I can do for you.

564
00:27:15,760 --> 00:27:19,360
And I know how to make plenty of healthy dishes to keep your camera ready.

565
00:27:19,360 --> 00:27:35,800
So Natalie, I heard that you wanted to be an actress ever since you were a little girl.

566
00:27:36,800 --> 00:27:38,020
Yes, that's right.

567
00:27:38,020 --> 00:27:40,400
Well then, I hope you book something real soon.

568
00:27:41,080 --> 00:27:41,420
Yeah!

569
00:27:44,380 --> 00:27:48,640
Even the smallest star in the sky shines like an angel from the heavens!

570
00:27:48,920 --> 00:27:52,200
No, no, no. Do you even know what you're saying? You sound like you're reading.

571
00:27:52,260 --> 00:27:53,840
Right! I'm so sorry.

572
00:27:57,400 --> 00:27:58,860
Here. You thirsty?

573
00:27:59,960 --> 00:28:01,320
Yes, thank you so much.

574
00:28:03,240 --> 00:28:05,220
Oh no! Puffo has arrived!

575
00:28:05,880 --> 00:28:06,980
So, how's it going?

576
00:28:07,420 --> 00:28:07,740
Natalie.

577
00:28:08,020 --> 00:28:08,780
Show me your face.

578
00:28:10,860 --> 00:28:11,060
Oh!

579
00:28:11,580 --> 00:28:12,540
What is she doing?

580
00:28:14,060 --> 00:28:14,960
Very good.

581
00:28:15,200 --> 00:28:16,360
She's almost ready.

582
00:28:18,100 --> 00:28:18,460
Huh?

583
00:28:38,020 --> 00:28:51,120
Yes, got it.

584
00:28:51,120 --> 00:28:53,260
Oh, a haircut.

585
00:28:53,260 --> 00:28:55,520
All right, I will let her know.

586
00:28:55,520 --> 00:28:56,520
Don't you worry, okay?

587
00:28:56,520 --> 00:28:59,020
You're finally making a move at last, huh, Pumbo?

588
00:28:59,020 --> 00:29:14,980
Oh, Natalie, Miss Pumbo would like to see you at the studio tomorrow. Also, I got my hair cut just like you asked me to.

589
00:29:14,980 --> 00:29:16,940
I got my hair cut just like you asked me to.

590
00:29:16,940 --> 00:29:19,700
I got my hair cut just like you asked me to.

591
00:29:19,700 --> 00:29:24,100
Director Jean!

592
00:29:24,800 --> 00:29:25,920
What? Director?

593
00:29:26,580 --> 00:29:27,940
Oh, wait. That's me.

594
00:29:28,260 --> 00:29:30,560
I can't believe this is happening to us.

595
00:29:30,720 --> 00:29:33,100
I feel so giddy that I'm trying not to faint.

596
00:29:33,320 --> 00:29:34,200
Yeah, me too.

597
00:29:34,680 --> 00:29:35,980
I'm so nauseous.

598
00:29:36,180 --> 00:29:36,940
Hey there.

599
00:29:38,620 --> 00:29:39,020
Mistia!

600
00:29:39,320 --> 00:29:42,600
You know, whether you two are ready or not, this movie is going to get made.

601
00:29:43,160 --> 00:29:45,500
This is your chance to fulfill your lifelong dreams.

602
00:29:45,900 --> 00:29:47,880
Don't just stand there. Go out there and network.

603
00:29:49,700 --> 00:29:51,780
Here I go!

604
00:29:55,380 --> 00:29:57,860
Okay, Jean. It's your turn now.

605
00:30:07,000 --> 00:30:09,860
You're Jean, the director, am I right?

606
00:30:12,700 --> 00:30:13,940
It's Martin!

607
00:30:14,800 --> 00:30:16,240
Best of luck.

608
00:30:16,760 --> 00:30:17,520
Right?

609
00:30:18,120 --> 00:30:19,640
Thanks for doing this.

610
00:30:19,700 --> 00:30:21,240
Ah, there you are.

611
00:30:21,780 --> 00:30:22,960
I don't believe my eyes.

612
00:30:23,560 --> 00:30:28,180
Two legends who between them have won six Nia Academy Awards are standing right before me.

613
00:30:29,480 --> 00:30:31,140
Good. Good to see you again, sir.

614
00:30:31,680 --> 00:30:31,880
Hmm?

615
00:30:32,400 --> 00:30:33,240
Wait a minute.

616
00:30:33,600 --> 00:30:36,100
You're a hawk and animal of the road warriors.

617
00:30:36,140 --> 00:30:36,600
I'm Jean.

618
00:30:36,860 --> 00:30:37,320
We've met.

619
00:30:37,320 --> 00:30:37,800
Yes, of course.

620
00:30:37,800 --> 00:30:39,000
Yes, of course.

621
00:30:39,120 --> 00:30:40,080
It's Jean, right?

622
00:30:40,480 --> 00:30:42,140
Congratulations, director.

623
00:30:42,920 --> 00:30:44,200
Thank you so much, sir.

624
00:30:45,240 --> 00:30:50,560
For a big star, Martin gets lonely easily, so no need to give him space.

625
00:30:51,000 --> 00:30:53,260
Try to engage with him as much as possible.

626
00:30:53,620 --> 00:30:54,500
Oh, right.

627
00:30:55,180 --> 00:30:55,660
Jean!

628
00:30:56,340 --> 00:30:56,680
Jean!

629
00:30:56,680 --> 00:30:58,520
Uh, director Corbett.

630
00:30:59,020 --> 00:31:00,300
Your first movie.

631
00:31:00,440 --> 00:31:00,860
Congratulations.

632
00:31:01,480 --> 00:31:04,580
Thanks, and congratulations to you on the success of Marine.

633
00:31:04,780 --> 00:31:05,360
No, no.

634
00:31:05,440 --> 00:31:07,040
My crew deserves all the credit.

635
00:31:07,540 --> 00:31:11,440
Hey, Jean, would you mind if I give you one piece of advice?

636
00:31:11,640 --> 00:31:13,260
Yes, of course you may.

637
00:31:13,800 --> 00:31:18,040
Since this is your first film and Martin is your star, it means you're going to be under

638
00:31:18,040 --> 00:31:19,100
a whole lot of pressure.

639
00:31:19,640 --> 00:31:23,420
If you try to please everyone, your movie's going to be a directionless mess.

640
00:31:24,060 --> 00:31:25,660
But here's how to fix that.

641
00:31:25,660 --> 00:31:29,720
All you have to do is think about the one person you want to show the movie to the most.

642
00:31:29,900 --> 00:31:34,220
And as long as you make it for them, your movie will end up with a laser-sharp focus.

643
00:31:34,380 --> 00:31:35,180
That makes sense.

644
00:31:36,420 --> 00:31:39,960
I've been pretty worried about screwing it all up, so that was helpful.

645
00:31:39,960 --> 00:31:41,760
What?

646
00:31:42,180 --> 00:31:44,380
She's the female lead, not you?

647
00:31:44,520 --> 00:31:46,320
Yeah, I'm actually not even in it.

648
00:31:46,660 --> 00:31:48,240
I'm going to be playing the female lead!

649
00:31:48,260 --> 00:31:48,740
Oh, man.

650
00:31:49,180 --> 00:31:50,480
What a disappointment.

651
00:31:51,400 --> 00:31:55,540
Anyway, the name's Martin Braddock, the best actor in the world.

652
00:31:55,800 --> 00:31:57,200
Shall we exchange socials?

653
00:31:57,220 --> 00:31:58,860
I don't have a smartphone, sorry.

654
00:32:02,460 --> 00:32:06,220
Oh, Martin was so disappointed that I'm the lead.

655
00:32:06,520 --> 00:32:08,420
Could that mean I'm not good enough?

656
00:32:08,420 --> 00:32:09,900
Oh, Director Jean!

657
00:32:10,900 --> 00:32:12,840
I get heartburn when I hear that.

658
00:32:15,880 --> 00:32:17,400
Can I ask you something?

659
00:32:17,660 --> 00:32:18,060
Yes?

660
00:32:18,060 --> 00:32:22,300
Is it weird to have me playing your female lead?

661
00:32:23,180 --> 00:32:25,160
Maybe I'm not attractive enough.

662
00:32:27,840 --> 00:32:31,260
I'm so nervous about this that part of me wants to run away.

663
00:32:31,880 --> 00:32:35,760
But when I think about it, I'd just be running away from reality.

664
00:32:36,600 --> 00:32:40,200
And where would I run to, since this is the only place I belong?

665
00:32:40,200 --> 00:32:44,940
So I only have two choices.

666
00:32:45,700 --> 00:32:47,180
Make the movie, or die.

667
00:32:48,120 --> 00:32:50,580
And so, I'm doing this no matter what.

668
00:32:50,880 --> 00:32:51,680
I won't run.

669
00:32:52,020 --> 00:32:52,580
I won't!

670
00:32:52,580 --> 00:32:58,840
Blue skies.

671
00:33:01,040 --> 00:33:03,040
Cornfields as far as the eye can see.

672
00:33:05,100 --> 00:33:06,960
That's all there is in my hometown.

673
00:33:06,960 --> 00:33:11,720
And that's the reason I loved movies so much.

674
00:33:12,780 --> 00:33:14,440
They were a way for me to escape.

675
00:33:14,980 --> 00:33:16,200
A way for me to dream.

676
00:33:16,700 --> 00:33:18,840
One day, I'm going to become an actress!

677
00:33:18,840 --> 00:33:23,720
Don't worry, my dear.

678
00:33:23,940 --> 00:33:26,960
You'll make a wonderful actress one day, Natalie.

679
00:33:28,720 --> 00:33:32,120
Ever since that day, I worked as hard as I could.

680
00:33:32,660 --> 00:33:36,120
I saved up all my money so that I could come here to N'yallywood.

681
00:33:36,820 --> 00:33:38,280
This is my big break.

682
00:33:38,700 --> 00:33:40,440
It's also my whole life.

683
00:33:41,040 --> 00:33:42,840
Ah, you know...

684
00:33:43,360 --> 00:33:43,920
Yes?

685
00:33:44,280 --> 00:33:46,840
I just remembered something Pompo said to me.

686
00:33:46,840 --> 00:33:50,660
She said as long as your lead actress is attractive,

687
00:33:50,860 --> 00:33:52,100
you've nothing to worry about.

688
00:33:52,280 --> 00:33:53,380
Because your movie will be a hit.

689
00:33:55,580 --> 00:33:58,320
You were hand-picked by Pompo herself.

690
00:33:58,680 --> 00:34:01,940
So you're attractive because you're attractive enough to be a lead actress.

691
00:34:02,540 --> 00:34:03,000
You know?

692
00:34:05,080 --> 00:34:08,660
And regardless, I can't see anyone else in the role of Lily.

693
00:34:09,080 --> 00:34:10,340
You don't need to worry.

694
00:34:10,560 --> 00:34:11,960
Just let me take care of the rest.

695
00:34:16,840 --> 00:34:24,460
Mm, all right.

696
00:34:25,080 --> 00:34:27,300
Thank you for the confidence.

697
00:34:27,860 --> 00:34:29,760
Let's make a movie, director!

698
00:34:30,440 --> 00:34:30,660
Huh?

699
00:34:31,000 --> 00:34:31,600
Yes?

700
00:34:31,600 --> 00:34:31,640
Yes?

701
00:34:31,640 --> 00:34:41,700
What?

702
00:34:41,860 --> 00:34:42,480
You're not sleeping?

703
00:34:43,080 --> 00:34:46,220
Oh, well, I'm just going over some notes from the location manager.

704
00:34:46,880 --> 00:34:48,700
Make sure to get plenty of rest.

705
00:34:49,080 --> 00:34:51,280
Don't forget, that's also part of your job.

706
00:34:51,280 --> 00:34:59,780
Sorry, I need to go to the restroom.

707
00:35:00,020 --> 00:35:01,180
You just went, Alan.

708
00:35:01,500 --> 00:35:02,440
Now you look here.

709
00:35:02,620 --> 00:35:04,200
This is a huge contract for us.

710
00:35:04,320 --> 00:35:05,100
Don't mess it up.

711
00:35:05,200 --> 00:35:05,740
Got that?

712
00:35:06,740 --> 00:35:07,820
I won't.

713
00:35:09,260 --> 00:35:09,960
We'll see.

714
00:35:09,960 --> 00:35:29,300
I know him.

715
00:35:29,980 --> 00:35:30,760
But how?

716
00:35:30,760 --> 00:35:37,620
Hello!

717
00:35:38,120 --> 00:35:40,020
Bumbo has arrived in Switzerland!

718
00:35:41,440 --> 00:35:43,600
Oh, this is great.

719
00:35:44,060 --> 00:35:49,840
The despondent Dalbert lands in Switzerland and is moved to tears by the splendor of the Alps.

720
00:35:50,000 --> 00:35:51,360
That is such a great idea.

721
00:35:51,900 --> 00:35:52,840
I know, right?

722
00:35:53,120 --> 00:35:54,560
No, it won't work.

723
00:35:54,680 --> 00:35:54,880
What?

724
00:35:54,880 --> 00:35:59,540
When he first arrives here, his heart is closed off to the outside world.

725
00:35:59,700 --> 00:36:01,540
He's not even capable of noticing the scenery.

726
00:36:01,940 --> 00:36:02,380
Oh.

727
00:36:04,380 --> 00:36:04,820
Ah!

728
00:36:07,060 --> 00:36:07,500
Sorry!

729
00:36:07,900 --> 00:36:10,500
I have no right to challenge any of your creative ideas!

730
00:36:10,700 --> 00:36:11,760
Nah, it's fine.

731
00:36:11,900 --> 00:36:13,220
You're the director, after all.

732
00:36:13,260 --> 00:36:14,800
Uh, yes, sir.

733
00:36:14,900 --> 00:36:17,340
It takes a village to make one of these little movies.

734
00:36:17,700 --> 00:36:21,140
Just know that I will never hesitate to give you my opinion.

735
00:36:21,140 --> 00:36:23,980
And it's your job to take it or leave it.

736
00:36:23,980 --> 00:36:24,980
Uh, right.

737
00:36:25,660 --> 00:36:28,840
Everyone, feel free to give your creative input.

738
00:36:28,940 --> 00:36:29,220
Okay!

739
00:36:29,560 --> 00:36:33,860
There are benefits to having veteran actors in your cast.

740
00:36:43,220 --> 00:36:45,140
Look how far I've come, Grandma.

741
00:36:46,080 --> 00:36:48,640
And Mistia, I'll do my best.

742
00:36:49,300 --> 00:36:51,680
Scene 32, shot one, take one.

743
00:36:51,960 --> 00:36:53,600
Exterior, meadow, Alps.

744
00:36:53,600 --> 00:36:55,220
We see the heartbroken Delbert.

745
00:36:55,440 --> 00:36:57,020
He meets Lily for the first time.

746
00:36:57,020 --> 00:36:57,560
Ready?

747
00:36:58,560 --> 00:36:59,280
Got it.

748
00:37:03,460 --> 00:37:03,940
Rolling!

749
00:37:04,940 --> 00:37:05,420
Action!

750
00:37:05,420 --> 00:37:15,400
This is the power of the best actor in the world.

751
00:37:16,340 --> 00:37:21,800
He's usually so lively, but as soon as the cameras rolled, he embodied despondency.

752
00:37:23,220 --> 00:37:28,800
However, what's even more surprising, though, is Lily.

753
00:37:28,800 --> 00:37:32,800
Her star quality is undeniable.

754
00:37:36,800 --> 00:37:39,400
She's perfect, because I wrote it for her.

755
00:37:39,400 --> 00:37:43,560
This is what it looks like when a script is written for an actor.

756
00:37:48,820 --> 00:37:55,340
So, Martin, will you be going back to Nellywood to shoot the orchestra scene after we're done filming here?

757
00:37:55,520 --> 00:37:56,320
That's the plan.

758
00:37:56,320 --> 00:37:56,840
How?

759
00:37:56,840 --> 00:37:59,620
Do you have to go through conductor training or anything?

760
00:37:59,940 --> 00:38:01,540
Actually, it's not a problem.

761
00:38:02,200 --> 00:38:03,980
Martin has played a conductor twice previously.

762
00:38:04,860 --> 00:38:08,900
In the climax of the film, Walter, he had to conduct a live, full orchestra.

763
00:38:09,560 --> 00:38:12,980
The scene was a single shot lasting six minutes and 40 seconds.

764
00:38:13,660 --> 00:38:15,200
And it made cinematic history.

765
00:38:15,760 --> 00:38:19,200
Professional musicians praised his performance, saying it was perfect.

766
00:38:19,200 --> 00:38:22,320
So, I'm sure he'll remember how to do it with very little coaching.

767
00:38:23,780 --> 00:38:24,040
Uh.

768
00:38:26,200 --> 00:38:27,860
Sorry, did I say something wrong?

769
00:38:27,980 --> 00:38:29,820
Oh, I'm speechless.

770
00:38:30,320 --> 00:38:31,660
That's Jean for you.

771
00:38:31,800 --> 00:38:33,140
You really are amazing.

772
00:38:33,620 --> 00:38:35,740
You know everything there is about movies.

773
00:38:35,920 --> 00:38:37,960
Well, it's all I have.

774
00:38:38,020 --> 00:38:42,060
Honestly, I'm happy and shocked that you're familiar with one of my older films.

775
00:38:42,220 --> 00:38:43,500
Well, of course I am.

776
00:38:43,660 --> 00:38:44,920
I've seen every one of your films.

777
00:38:45,020 --> 00:38:46,020
They're all masterpieces.

778
00:38:46,720 --> 00:38:47,880
I like you.

779
00:38:47,880 --> 00:38:50,560
Let's call it a day and drink until dawn.

780
00:38:50,820 --> 00:38:51,260
Oh, there we are.

781
00:38:54,700 --> 00:38:56,880
So, let's frame it with the sun on the right.

782
00:38:57,040 --> 00:38:59,260
But I also want the shot to be a little backlit.

783
00:38:59,340 --> 00:38:59,780
You got that?

784
00:39:00,440 --> 00:39:03,180
The director's really particular about the lighting.

785
00:39:03,500 --> 00:39:04,780
He's done so many setups.

786
00:39:05,060 --> 00:39:08,120
It's the scene where you take Delbert for a walk with all the goats.

787
00:39:09,080 --> 00:39:12,200
My guess is he just wants to do the whole thing in a single take.

788
00:39:12,620 --> 00:39:13,020
Oh.

789
00:39:14,120 --> 00:39:14,300
Hmm?

790
00:39:16,040 --> 00:39:16,480
Huh?

791
00:39:17,880 --> 00:39:22,400
I'm so sorry about this.

792
00:39:22,520 --> 00:39:24,400
The roof fell in and spooked them.

793
00:39:25,040 --> 00:39:27,160
We patched it up as best we could, but...

794
00:39:27,160 --> 00:39:29,480
It was pretty rickety to start with.

795
00:39:30,540 --> 00:39:32,980
But I thought there were supposed to be more goats.

796
00:39:33,220 --> 00:39:34,320
Well, you see...

797
00:39:34,320 --> 00:39:37,900
They were eaten by wolves?

798
00:39:38,840 --> 00:39:40,020
Great things!

799
00:39:40,420 --> 00:39:42,060
That means we don't have enough goats.

800
00:39:42,180 --> 00:39:43,000
What do we do now?

801
00:39:43,260 --> 00:39:44,480
What did the goat herder say?

802
00:39:44,600 --> 00:39:45,840
It's impossible to get more.

803
00:39:45,840 --> 00:39:48,280
Should we postpone then?

804
00:39:48,640 --> 00:39:51,240
Except we have a limited number of shooting days at this location.

805
00:39:51,560 --> 00:39:52,860
And the weather's about to change.

806
00:39:54,000 --> 00:39:55,480
The fog's rolling in.

807
00:39:56,440 --> 00:39:57,140
Fog, huh?

808
00:40:00,140 --> 00:40:02,020
Do we have a smoke machine handy?

809
00:40:02,020 --> 00:40:15,340
But why?

810
00:40:15,340 --> 00:40:28,840
It's okay. Don't be afraid.

811
00:40:30,680 --> 00:40:32,180
Come. This way.

812
00:40:37,600 --> 00:40:39,820
The smoke was a great idea.

813
00:40:40,080 --> 00:40:42,260
And the goats were the right amount of scary.

814
00:40:42,260 --> 00:40:45,860
There also ended up being enough of them with the cutouts we made.

815
00:40:46,880 --> 00:40:50,240
The script merely described Delbear and Lily going for a walk.

816
00:40:52,000 --> 00:40:53,340
Way to go, Gene!

817
00:41:01,880 --> 00:41:03,700
Well, today's a wash.

818
00:41:03,840 --> 00:41:06,020
You want to try to shoot all the interiors instead?

819
00:41:12,260 --> 00:41:15,860
Gene? Gene, hey!

820
00:41:17,080 --> 00:41:18,240
What do you say?

821
00:41:18,960 --> 00:41:22,540
Uh, could I shoot an additional scene that's not in the script?

822
00:41:25,160 --> 00:41:29,660
You're a funny guy. You don't gotta ask me. You're the boss after all.

823
00:41:29,660 --> 00:41:35,360
Why do I have to do this?

824
00:41:35,620 --> 00:41:36,780
This is the neat thing.

825
00:41:37,000 --> 00:41:38,760
More working and less smoking.

826
00:41:39,460 --> 00:41:42,520
And hurry it up before one of the goats catches a cold.

827
00:41:42,620 --> 00:41:43,840
Got it. I got it.

828
