1417
01:14:32,020 --> 01:14:33,120
Turn off the stream!

1418
01:14:33,120 --> 01:14:36,660
A certain someone informed me of this, and I'm glad they did.

1419
01:14:38,220 --> 01:14:39,300
I was watching.

1420
01:14:39,300 --> 01:14:43,360
You know, it's by far the best presentation I've seen in a long time.

1421
01:14:43,360 --> 01:14:47,040
And it took resolve and great courage in order to pull it off.

1422
01:14:48,040 --> 01:14:50,500
This little project has a lot of potential.

1423
01:14:51,500 --> 01:14:54,100
We'll invest ten times the crowdfunding amount.

1424
01:14:54,400 --> 01:14:55,340
How's that sound?

1425
01:14:56,380 --> 01:14:57,380
But, sir...

1426
01:14:57,380 --> 01:15:00,900
You're using past indices as indicators of potential growth.

1427
01:15:00,980 --> 01:15:03,420
But you're ignoring a very important element.

1428
01:15:03,540 --> 01:15:04,780
What do you mean?

1429
01:15:04,780 --> 01:15:10,120
Take a look at this.

1430
01:15:10,480 --> 01:15:11,920
Notice a spike in the funding.

1431
01:15:12,660 --> 01:15:15,800
Any of you want to guess what happened at that moment to motivate that spike?

1432
01:15:17,200 --> 01:15:21,740
It's the moment when Gene Feeney and Alan Gardner were pouring their hearts out to us.

1433
01:15:24,340 --> 01:15:27,500
Assessing potential means looking towards the future.

1434
01:15:28,900 --> 01:15:32,940
By investing in their dreams, they're investing in their future.

1435
01:15:34,780 --> 01:15:36,220
Even so...

1436
01:15:36,220 --> 01:15:40,020
And the Ollywood Bank invests in people who will invest in their dreams.

1437
01:15:40,220 --> 01:15:41,420
That is our motto.

1438
01:15:41,860 --> 01:15:43,720
Hold on. Since when is that our motto?

1439
01:15:44,460 --> 01:15:45,320
Since now.

1440
01:15:45,400 --> 01:15:45,620
What?

1441
01:15:47,000 --> 01:15:50,920
And Alan, you've got a very bright future ahead of you.

1442
01:15:56,540 --> 01:15:57,600
Oh, yes!

1443
01:16:03,600 --> 01:16:04,640
Nicely done.

1444
01:16:04,780 --> 01:16:06,680
Thank you so much, sir.

1445
01:16:06,680 --> 01:16:07,880
Oh, man.

1446
01:16:07,880 --> 01:16:11,460
I can't remember the last time we've had such a crazy meeting.

1447
01:16:11,460 --> 01:16:15,220
It reminds me of back when the president was still a junior executive.

1448
01:16:16,300 --> 01:16:17,200
We'll invest!

1449
01:16:17,800 --> 01:16:19,160
Oh, that was thrilling!

1450
01:16:19,160 --> 01:16:35,540
I really appreciate you all for coming back to shoot this additional scene.

1451
01:16:35,540 --> 01:16:37,440
Everyone wins it for the world!

1452
01:16:37,440 --> 01:16:39,440
Why are you standing around?

1453
01:16:39,440 --> 01:16:43,220
Everyone's here because we've got a crucial scene to shoot, right?

1454
01:16:46,220 --> 01:16:47,360
Oh, everyone.

1455
01:16:47,360 --> 01:16:49,480
Thank you so much.

1456
01:16:49,480 --> 01:16:54,380
The scene we'll be shooting is a flashback to when Dalbert loses his family.

1457
01:16:54,380 --> 01:16:56,280
So, who's playing my wife?

1458
01:16:56,280 --> 01:16:57,280
Who's playing my wife?

1459
01:16:57,280 --> 01:16:58,080
That would be me.

1460
01:16:58,080 --> 01:16:58,380
That would be me.

1461
